    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) standing as the clear priority start. His elite speed profile\u2014amplified by a rare dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable matchup against Brandon Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery\u2014makes him the primary engine for our scarce stolen base category. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (77.56) and **Junior Caminero** (76.90) offer high-floor production, with **Yordan Alvarez** benefiting from an elite 0.458 xwOBA and **Junior Caminero** slotted into a favorable #3 hole. **Lars Nootbaar** (64.56) also emerges as a top-tier play; while Clay Holmes is a difficult arm, the combination of a leadoff spot and a strong platoon edge gives him significant potential to generate runs despite the pitching difficulty.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Chase Meidroth** (36.09), who fell well below our 40.0 efficiency threshold primarily due to a brutal matchup against Jacob deGrom. While **Chase Meidroth** is a capable utility piece, the sheer talent gap presented by deGrom\u2019s skill profile resulted in a 19-point drop in expected performance, making him an easy scratch for our more optimized lineup slots. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Pedro Ramirez**. While **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** are locked in as core contributors, they face George Kirby, an elite arm who demands caution. **Hector Rodriguez** remains an interesting deep-roster play; his score of 57.54 is bolstered significantly by a 16-point boost for his matchup against Adrian Houser and favorable wind conditions, though his position at the bottom of the order tempers his ceiling. We will monitor for any late scratches, but as it stands, the roster is positioned to prioritize efficiency in the SB category without sacrificing power.",
